    "title": "Morningside football gears up for top-10 battle with Dordt, GPAC title hangs in the balance - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Anthony Mitchell ,\n47 minutes ago\nSIOUX CITY, Iowa (KCAU) – The Morningside Mustangs are getting ready for battle on Saturday as the final week of the conference title remains in the balance headed into the regular season finale.\n#9 Morningside enters the week with an 8-1 GPAC record, trailing only its opponent on Saturday in the #6 Dordt Defenders.\nThe ‘Stangs have embraced the challenge and hope its preparation throughout the week translates to Saturday success.\n“We’ve worked all year for an opportunity like this and we’ve just got to take advantage of it. We’ve put in a good week of prep already and we need another good day today, but this is what you live for right here. Those emotions are very real. Once November comes, it’s getting realer and realer every game. We know every single game from here on out, if we want to be champions, is going to be tough,” Morningside quarterback Zack Chevalier said.\n“The last time we played them here, we committed a lot of turnovers, we played very sloppy, and we turned the ball over. We talked about those things on offense and on defense we need to create turnovers and find ways to get off the field,” Morningside head coach Steve Ryan mentioned.\nKickoff at Elwood Olsen Stadium is scheduled for 1 p.m.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
